¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙîThey are turned back to the iniquities of their forefathers, which refused to hear my words; and they went after other gods to serve them: the house of Israel and the house of Judah have broken my covenant which I made with their fathers.¦layout ªlast_verse
…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬Therefore thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will bring evil upon them, which they shall not be able to escape; and though they shall cry unto me, I will not hearken unto them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµThen shall the cities of Judah and inhabitants of Jerusalem go, and cry unto the gods unto whom they offer incense: but they shall not save them at all in the time of their trouble.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÎFor according to the number of thy cities were thy gods, O Judah; and according to the number of the streets of Jerusalem have ye set up altars to that shameful thing, even altars to burn incense unto Baal.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ Therefore pray not thou for this people, neither lift up a cry or prayer for them: for I will not hear them in the time that they cry unto me for their trouble.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨What hath my beloved to do in mine house, seeing she hath wrought lewdness with many, and the holy flesh is passed from thee? when thou doest evil, then thou rejoicest.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªThe LORD called thy name, A green olive tree, fair, and of goodly fruit: with the noise of a great tumult he hath kindled fire upon it, and the branches of it are broken.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙéFor the LORD of hosts, that planted thee, hath pronounced evil against thee, for the evil of the house of Israel and of the house of Judah, which they have done against themselves to provoke me to anger in offering incense unto Baal.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^And the LORD hath given me knowledge of it, and I know it: then thou shewedst me their doings.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚBut I was like a lamb or an ox that is brought to the slaughter; and I knew not that they had devised devices against me, saying, Let us destroy the tree with the fruit thereof, and let us cut him off from the land of the living, that his name may be no more remembered.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut, O LORD of hosts, that judgest righteously, that triest the reins and the heart, let me see thy vengeance on them: for unto thee have I revealed my cause.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–Therefore thus saith the LORD of the men of Anathoth, that seek thy life, saying, Prophesy not in the name of the LORD, that thou die not by our hand:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtherefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, Behold, I will punish them: the young men shall die by the sword; their sons and their daughters shall die by famine:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyand there shall be no remnant of them: for I will bring evil upon the men of Anathoth, even the year of their visitation.¦layout ªlast_verse